{"id":23010,"title":"Flow Visualization Techniques for CDF using Volume Rendering","url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/790542","final_url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/790542","year":2000,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"4e432c12e722dd355e309b0147b4172b127cf76fb14637784661d3de51cca192","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793063379.546296,"text_chars":39088,"abstract":"As simulations have migrated towards three-dimensions, new tools for examining the resulting complex datasets have been required. Much progress has been achieved in the area of scientific visualization towards this goal. However, most of the research has focused on the representation and understanding of a single scalar field. Some nice results have been achieved for vector or flow fields. This paper reviews several of these techniques, organizes them by their approach and complexity and presents some observations on their benefits and limitations. Several example images are used to highlight the character of these techniques.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/790542","https://osti.gov/biblio/790542","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/m2/1/high_res_d/790542.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=volume data compression rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=smoke rendering volume","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=scientific volume visualization","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=fluid simulation volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=vector field volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=tensor field visualization volume","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=volumetric 3d display rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=simulation data volume visualization","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=flow visualization volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=adaptive resolution volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=image order volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=westover back-to-front","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=model parallel volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=differential sampling volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=adaptive step size volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=direct volume rendering tetrahedra","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=spatial convolution volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc716427/?q=analytical vector fields volume rendering"],"cited_by":[{"path":"23-splatting.md","name":"Splatting","k":20},{"path":"3857-tensorf-vm.md","name":"TensoRF-VM","k":1},{"path":"3857-illumination-and-tone-shading-models.md","name":"Illumination and Tone Shading Models","k":1},{"path":"2959-spot-noise.md","name":"Spot Noise","k":1},{"path":"6056-hardware-shading-via-pixel-texture.md","name":"Hardware Shading via Pixel Texture","k":4},{"path":"7693-vector-icon-volume-rendering.md","name":"Vector Icon Volume Rendering","k":1},{"path":"7700-stream-balls.md","name":"Stream-Balls","k":1},{"path":"7696-stream-surfaces.md","name":"Stream Surfaces","k":1},{"path":"7721-lic-on-stream-surfaces.md","name":"LIC on Stream Surfaces","k":1},{"path":"7940-line-integral-convolution-lic.md","name":"Line Integral Convolution (LIC)","k":1},{"path":"7690-flow-volumes.md","name":"Flow Volumes","k":1},{"path":"7694-vector-topology-analysis.md","name":"Vector Topology Analysis","k":1}]}